; hall.moritz - a patch for the sound editor's Process > A patch...: the selection in a hall, a
; reverb~ of 3 s (a stereo Freeverb) on each channel, the left one's left output and the right one's
; right output, with the dry sound. The editor renders the selection through the patch and then the
; tail its dialog asks for (2 s at first; silence at its end is left out): replacing the selection,
; the hall's tail rings on over what follows it (mixed; the sound grows only past its end). For the
; whole decay, give a tail as long as it (3 s here). Change reverb~'s arguments: the mix (0 dry to 1
; wet) and the decay in seconds.
(patch
  (obj title comment "Process > A patch...: the selection in a hall (reverb~ 0.35 3)" (pos 20 12))
  (obj inl inlet~ (pos 20 50))
  (obj inr inlet~ (pos 250 50))
  (obj rl reverb~ 0.35 3 (pos 20 100))
  (obj rr reverb~ 0.35 3 (pos 250 100))
  (obj cr comment "reverb~ mix decay(s): each channel its own hall, kept apart" (pos 20 135))
  (obj outl outlet~ (pos 20 170))
  (obj outr outlet~ (pos 250 170))
  (connect inl 0 rl 0)
  (connect inr 0 rr 0)
  (connect rl 0 outl 0)
  (connect rr 1 outr 0))
